# Day 14

**25km / 7.5 hours**

This section is awkward to work out how far to go with the accommodation options available. I decided on two options, depending on how nice Helena Bay looked. I left The Farm, where I was staying, and walked along the road yet again until eventually arriving at Helena Bay. 

![The view from Helena Bay](./helena-bay.jpg)

However at this point it was too early in the day and the bay wasn't that nice so I continued on the road. It's hard to imagine some interesting thing to say about walking on the road since it's quite monotonous, the surface is mostly the same. The only interesting thing was that after around 300km of walking, I finally saw billboards for a new electorate. It's election season here and there are electorates with a local member of parliament and so far I've seen heaps of billboards for the [Northland electorate](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Northland_(electorate)) but now we're finally getting Whangārei billboards.

After continuing, I got to the actual ridge track which was a relief after being on the road, although it's a lot tougher since there's much more elevation change. It was much better maintained with proper stairs and boardwalk and even the luxury of benches along the way. There were nice trees, birds and views which is all you can ask for. 

![The view of the coast along the way](./coast-view.jpg)

After coming out of the forest and some farmland featuring some eager cows I came to a small campsite to stop for the day. It only had a water tank that was awkward to access and a bench but that was enough for a pleasant enough night.